1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.260
本吉奥: Yes, my definition of learning is not the kind of learning that people think about when they're in school and listening to a teacher. Learning is something we do all the time.
是的。我对学习的定义，并不是人们想到的那种坐在学校里，听老师讲课的学习。学习是我们一直都在做的事情。

2
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:19.550
本吉奥: Our brain is changing all the time in response to what we're seeing, experiencing. And it's an adaptation.
我们的大脑会随着所见、所经历的一切不断改变。这是一种适应。

3
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:28.460
本吉奥: And we are not just storing in our brain our experiences, it's not learning by heart, that's easy,
我们不只是把经历储存在大脑里。学习不等于死记硬背，后者很容易。

4
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.940
本吉奥: a file in a computer is like learning by heart. You can store facts.
计算机中的一个文件，就像死记硬背一样：你可以把事实存进去。

5
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:38.220
本吉奥: But that's trivial, that's not what learning really is about.
但那很简单，并不是学习真正的含义。

6
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:53.410
本吉奥: Learning is about integrating the information we are getting through experience into some more abstract form that allows us to take good decisions. That allow us to predict what will happen next.
学习，是把我们通过经验获得的信息整合成某种更抽象的形式，使我们能够做出好的决策，预测接下来会发生什么，

7
00:00:53.410 --> 00:01:02.340
本吉奥: That allow us to understand the connections between things we've seen. So, that's what learning is really about.
理解我们见过的事物之间的联系。这才是学习真正的含义。

8
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.750
本吉奥: In my field, we talk about the notion of generalization.
在我所在的领域，我们会谈到‘泛化’这个概念。

9
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:15.970
本吉奥: So, the machine can generalize from things it has seen and learned from, to new situations.
机器能够从它见过并学过的东西，推广到新的情境。

10
00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.380
本吉奥: That's the kind of learning we talk about in my field.
这就是我们这个领域所说的学习。

11
00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:36.590
本吉奥: And the way we typically do it in machines and how we think it's happening in the brain is that it's a slow, gradual process. Each time you live an experience, one second of your life, there's gonna be some changes in your brain.
我们在机器中通常采用的方式，以及我们认为大脑中发生的过程，都是缓慢的，渐进的过程。每当你有一段经历，生活过去一秒钟，你的大脑都会发生一些改变。

12
00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:47.780
本吉奥: Small changes. So it's like your whole system is gradually shifting towards what would make it take better decisions.
小小的改变。就像整个系统逐渐调整，让自己能够做出更好的决策。

13
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.170
本吉奥: So that's how you get to be intelligent, right?
所以，这就是你变得聪明的方式，对吧？

14
00:01:50.170 --> 00:02:07.330
本吉奥: Because you learn, meaning you changed the way you perceive and act, so that next time you would see something, you will have some experience similar to what happened before, you would act better or you would predict better what would have happened.
因为你在学习，也就是改变自己感知与行动的方式。这样，下次你再看到某件事，再经历与过去相似的情况时，你就会采取更好的行动，或者更准确地预测会发生什么。
